WEBVTT

00:05.800 --> 00:09.080
Education and training can help
you feel more confident and

00:09.080 --> 00:12.520
enable you to achieve
successful catheterization.

00:12.520 --> 00:16.200
You can use this step by step
video as support and follow-up

00:16.200 --> 00:18.040
on any training provided.

00:18.040 --> 00:21.800
Always follow the advice and
instructions provided by a clinician,

00:21.800 --> 00:26.400
which are tailored to your individual
medical and lifestyle needs.

00:26.400 --> 00:29.760
So what is intermittent catheterization?

00:29.760 --> 00:33.280
Intermittent catheterization
helps empty your bladder when

00:33.280 --> 00:35.680
your body can't do it on its own.

00:35.680 --> 00:38.880
It involves emptying your
bladder regularly with a hollow

00:38.880 --> 00:42.000
tube with drainage
holes, a catheter.

00:42.000 --> 00:44.640
The catheter is inserted
in your urethra,

00:44.640 --> 00:47.200
which is the tube between
the bladder and the exit,

00:47.200 --> 00:53.360
allowing the urine to flow
down the catheter and out.

00:53.360 --> 00:56.720
Let's briefly go through the
body parts involved in the

00:56.720 --> 00:58.800
urinary system.

00:58.800 --> 00:59.760
Kidney.

00:59.760 --> 01:03.520
Your kidneys are two small bean
shaped organs that clean your

01:03.520 --> 01:05.320
blood and make urine.

01:05.640 --> 01:06.920
Ureter.

01:06.920 --> 01:10.760
The ureters are thin tubes that
carry urine from the kidneys

01:10.760 --> 01:12.840
down to the bladder.

01:12.840 --> 01:14.040
Bladder.

01:14.040 --> 01:17.240
The bladder is a hollow
stretchy organ in your lower

01:17.240 --> 01:19.480
belly that stores urine.

01:19.480 --> 01:20.920
Urethra.

01:20.920 --> 01:24.520
The urethra is the tube that
carries urine from the bladder

01:24.520 --> 01:26.240
out of the body.

01:26.360 --> 01:31.080
And finally, the
urethral opening.

01:31.080 --> 01:34.640
It is quite usual to feel a
little anxious or worried when

01:34.640 --> 01:37.040
starting something new
for the first time,

01:37.040 --> 01:38.800
but with practice and support,

01:38.800 --> 01:41.440
you will soon become more
confident with intermittent

01:41.440 --> 01:44.880
catheterization and it will
soon become a natural part of

01:44.880 --> 01:46.800
your daily routine.

01:46.800 --> 01:52.160
Now, let's talk through how to
use LoFric Elle step by step.

01:52.160 --> 01:55.920
Start by washing your hands
thoroughly with soap and water.

01:55.920 --> 01:59.280
You can also use cleansing
wipes if you don't have access

01:59.280 --> 02:00.800
to running water.

02:00.800 --> 02:04.160
Cleanse your hands again
after catheterization.

02:04.160 --> 02:05.920
Open the upper lid.

02:05.920 --> 02:10.480
Hold the catheter in one hand and
gently bend the upper part to open.

02:10.480 --> 02:12.640
Pull the catheter out.

02:12.640 --> 02:16.000
Connect the container to the
catheter with a gentle twist,

02:16.000 --> 02:19.920
making sure the arrow on
the container points down.

02:19.920 --> 02:24.240
LoFric Elle is an intermittent
catheter with a unique L-shaped

02:24.240 --> 02:27.800
handle that helps you
confidently locate the urethra.

02:27.800 --> 02:30.840
Sitting on the toilet
is ideal for doing IC,

02:30.840 --> 02:32.360
but if not possible,

02:32.360 --> 02:36.280
your clinician will help you find
a position that suits you best.

02:36.280 --> 02:39.800
Tilt your pelvis upwards
and spread your labia.

02:39.800 --> 02:43.000
Hold the handle with
your dominant hand.

02:43.000 --> 02:47.640
Gently and slowly guide the
catheter into the urethra.

02:47.640 --> 02:51.160
The urethral entrance is small
and sometimes hard to see and

02:51.160 --> 02:52.920
using a mirror can help.

02:52.920 --> 02:56.760
It is just above the vaginal
opening and below the clitoris.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.440
It is close to the anus,

02:58.440 --> 03:02.120
so keeping clean is important
to prevent infection.

03:02.120 --> 03:06.960
Once urine starts to flow, the
catheter is in the right place.

03:06.960 --> 03:11.440
Gently insert a little further to
ensure it's fully in your bladder.

03:11.440 --> 03:15.280
When urine stops, slowly
withdraw the catheter.

03:15.280 --> 03:19.640
If more urine flows, pause
and wait before continuing so

03:19.640 --> 03:21.480
the bladder is fully empty.

03:21.480 --> 03:24.360
The unique LoFric surface
coating will ensure that the

03:24.360 --> 03:27.400
catheter remains
smoothly lubricated.

03:27.400 --> 03:30.280
Put the catheter back
inside the container.

03:30.280 --> 03:34.000
Remember, LoFric Elle is a
urinary catheter designed to be

03:34.000 --> 03:35.920
used one time only.

03:35.920 --> 03:39.280
Dispose or carry it in
your bag until disposal.

03:39.280 --> 03:44.000
Please note, the lower
container is recyclable.

03:44.000 --> 03:47.600
How often you catheterize
will vary individually and

03:47.600 --> 03:50.160
also depend upon fluid intake.

03:50.160 --> 03:54.080
Your clinician will advise you
on the right regime for you.

03:54.080 --> 03:57.920
LoFric Elle is your versatile
single use intermittent

03:57.920 --> 04:02.560
catheter ready for you,
whatever your lifestyle needs.
